# Claude Code CLI - Complete API Reference
# Extracted from @anthropic-ai/claude-code v2.1.234
#
# Validation: search the release binary for the path literal.
#   scripts/extract-binary.sh 2.1.234           # paths + beta flags
#   scripts/extract-routes.py <binary> --all -  # method + path + beta + auth
#   scripts/extract-calls.py  <binary> out/     # byte window around a call site
# (Older wrapper packages shipped a readable cli.js; the same string patterns
#  apply to that file: rg '/api/oauth/profile' package/cli.js)
#
# See: WORKFLOW.md for the extraction workflow and precision requirements
#
# PROVENANCE (corrected at v2.1.234)
#
# Earlier revisions of this file warned that "header sets, request bodies and
# timeouts are NOT recoverable from a Bun binary" and carried them forward from
# v2.1.76, the last release with a readable bundle. That warning was wrong.
# The compiled binary embeds the entire minified JavaScript bundle as printable
# text -- one enormous line, which is why `rg -A/-B` context appeared to return
# nothing useful. Cut a byte window instead and the call site is right there:
#
#   fs.get("/v1/ultrareview/quota", {auth: "teleport-org", timeout: 3000})
#
# So from v2.1.234 on, methods, header sets, auth modes, timeouts and request
# bodies are read from the binary being documented, not carried forward.
# scripts/extract-routes.py does this mechanically for every call site.
#
# AUTH MODES
#
# axios call sites name their auth mode; the mode decides the entire header
# set. Verified in extractions/v2.1.234/calls/auth-modes.txt.
#
#   base builder (all modes below that use it):
#     Authorization: Bearer <token>
#     Content-Type: application/json
#     anthropic-version: 2023-06-01
#     anthropic-client-platform: <platform>
#
#   auth: "teleport-org"      base builder + x-organization-uuid: <orgUUID>.
#                             ALSO substitutes the literal ":orgUUID" in the
#                             path with the real org UUID -- that is why paths
#                             in the binary contain ":orgUUID" verbatim.
#   auth: "session-jwt"       Authorization: Bearer <session access token>. No
#                             other headers.
#   auth: "claude-ai-oauth"   Authorization: Bearer <oauth token>
#                             anthropic-beta: oauth-2025-04-20
#   auth: "none"              no auth headers.
#   auth: "async" / unset     resolved OAuth headers:
#                             Authorization: Bearer <oauth token>
#                             anthropic-beta: oauth-2025-04-20
#                             (or x-api-key when authenticated by API key)
#
# Two pre-flight refusals apply to every axios call before a request is made:
#   - essential-traffic-only mode blocks it unless the call sets
#     bypassEssentialTrafficOnly
#   - a non-first-party provider blocks it with reason "data-residency"
#
# Stainless SDK resources (/v1/*) take auth from the client rather than per
# call, and pin their own anthropic-beta flag per resource; those flags are in
# extractions/v2.1.234/raw/sdk_routes.tsv.
#
# ROUTE INDEX
#
# extractions/v2.1.234/raw/routes.tsv is the machine-readable index of all 236
# call sites: method, path, beta flag, auth mode, timeout, source. Sections
# below carry the prose and bodies; the TSV is the completeness check.

### ============================================================================
### VARIABLES
### ============================================================================

@baseUrl = https://api.anthropic.com
@platformUrl = https://platform.claude.com
@claudeAiUrl = https://claude.ai
@mcpProxyUrl = https://mcp-proxy.anthropic.com
@bridgeWsUrl = wss://bridge.claudeusercontent.com
@version = 2023-06-01
@oauthBeta = oauth-2025-04-20
@mcpBeta = mcp-servers-2025-12-04
@compactBeta = compact-2026-01-12
@clientId = 9d1c250a-e61b-44d9-88ed-5944d1962f5e
@stainlessVersion = 0.74.0
@managedAgentsBeta = managed-agents-2026-04-01
@cliVersion = 2.1.234

# Auth tokens (set these)
@accessToken = YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN
@sessionToken = YOUR_SESSION_ACCESS_TOKEN
@clientPlatform = cli
@apiKey = YOUR_API_KEY
@orgUuid = YOUR_ORG_UUID
@remoteSettingsChecksum = sha256:YOUR_CHECKSUM
@fileUuid = YOUR_FILE_UUID


### ============================================================================
### SECTION 1: OAUTH FLOW
### ============================================================================
# Pattern: rg "oauth/authorize|oauth/token" cli.js

### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1.1 Authorization URL (Browser redirect - not a direct request)
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pattern: rg "CONSOLE_AUTHORIZE_URL|CLAUDE_AI_AUTHORIZE_URL" cli.js
#
# Platform OAuth (v2.1.22+: console.anthropic.com → platform.claude.com):
#   https://platform.claude.com/oauth/authorize
#     ?code=true
#     &client_id=9d1c250a-e61b-44d9-88ed-5944d1962f5e
#     &response_type=code
#     &redirect_uri=http://localhost:{port}/callback
#     &scope=org:create_api_key user:profile user:inference user:sessions:claude_code user:mcp_servers user:file_upload
#     &code_challenge={base64url(sha256(code_verifier))}
#     &code_challenge_method=S256
#     &state={random_state}
#     [&orgUUID={org_uuid}]
#     [&login_hint={email}]      # from `claude auth login --email`
#     [&login_method=sso]        # from `claude auth login --sso`
#
# Claude.ai OAuth:
#   https://claude.ai/oauth/authorize
#     (same params as above)
#
# Scopes (pattern: rg '"user:inference"|"user:profile"|"user:sessions"|"user:mcp_servers"|"user:file_upload"' cli.js):
#   - user:inference         (required for API access; also marks the token
#                             as a Claude.ai subscription token)
#   - user:profile           (required for profile info)
#   - user:sessions:claude_code  (required for web sessions)
#   - user:mcp_servers       (required for MCP server access - NEW in v2.1.x)
#   - user:file_upload       (required for OAuth file transfer - NEW in v2.1.x)
#   - org:create_api_key     (required for API key creation)
#
# `claude setup-token` requests user:inference ONLY.

### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1.2 Token Exchange
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pattern: rg "grant_type.*authorization_code" cli.js

# @name tokenExchange
POST {{platformUrl}}/v1/oauth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "grant_type": "authorization_code",
    "code": "{{authCode}}",
    "redirect_uri": "http://localhost:{{port}}/callback",
    "client_id": "{{clientId}}",
    "code_verifier": "{{codeVerifier}}",
    "state": "{{state}}"
}

### Response:
# {
#   "access_token": "...",
#   "refresh_token": "...",
#   "expires_in": 3600,
#   "token_type": "Bearer",
#   "scope": "user:profile user:inference user:sessions:claude_code org:create_api_key"
# }

### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1.3 Token Refresh
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pattern: rg "grant_type.*refresh_token" cli.js

# @name tokenRefresh
POST {{platformUrl}}/v1/oauth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "grant_type": "refresh_token",
    "refresh_token": "{{refreshToken}}",
    "client_id": "{{clientId}}",
    "scope": "user:profile user:inference user:sessions:claude_code user:mcp_servers user:file_upload"
}

# The client always sends `scope` on refresh. When the stored token carries
# user:inference it sends the full 5-scope session set shown above,
# regardless of what was originally granted; otherwise it echoes the
# token's own recorded scopes.
# Refresh fires 5 minutes before expiry and is serialized across processes
# by a lock file (5 retries, 1-2s jittered backoff).


### ============================================================================
### SECTION 2: PROFILE & ACCOUNT
### ============================================================================

### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2.1 OAuth Profile (with Bearer token)
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pattern: rg '/api/oauth/profile' cli.js

# @name oauthProfile
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/oauth/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

### Response (corrected v2.1.76 - fields are NESTED under account/organization):
# {
#   "account": {
#     "uuid":         "...",
#     "email":        "...",
#     "display_name": "... | null",
#     "created_at":   "ISO-8601"
#   },
#   "organization": {
#     "uuid":                    "...",
#     "organization_type":       "claude_max|claude_pro|claude_enterprise|claude_team",
#     "rate_limit_tier":         "... | null",
#     "has_extra_usage_enabled": true|false|null,
#     "billing_type":            "stripe_subscription|stripe_subscription_contracted|apple_subscription|google_play_subscription|null",
#     "subscription_created_at": "ISO-8601 | null"
#   }
# }
#
# The profile does NOT return an organization name - that comes from 2.3.
# Note the field-name split: this endpoint uses account.email, while the
# token-exchange response uses account.email_address.
# Timeout 10000 ms. Errors are swallowed (returns undefined).

### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2.2 CLI Profile (with API key)
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pattern: rg "api/claude_cli_profile" cli.js

# @name cliProfile
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/claude_cli_profile?account_uuid={{accountUuid}}
x-api-key: {{apiKey}}
anthropic-beta: {{oauthBeta}}

### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2.3 Get User Roles
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pattern: rg "ROLES_URL" cli.js

# @name getUserRoles
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/oauth/claude_cli/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Response:
# {
#   "organization_role": "admin|member|...",
#   "workspace_role": "...",
#   "organization_name": "..."
# }

### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2.4 Create API Key
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pattern: rg "API_KEY_URL|create_api_key" cli.js

# @name createApiKey
# Authorization is the ONLY header. The body is null - no Content-Type is
# set and no JSON is sent. Requires org:create_api_key.
# Called only on the console login branch (token WITHOUT user:inference).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/oauth/claude_cli/create_api_key
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Response:
# {
#   "raw_key": "sk-ant-..."
# }

### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2.5 OAuth File Upload
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pattern: rg 'api/oauth/file_upload' cli.js
#
# Host is ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL || BASE_API_URL. Timeout 30000 ms.
# Success is strictly HTTP 201. Max 31457280 bytes (30 MiB), checked before
# reading; oversized files are silently skipped. Multipart is hand-built
# (not FormData), one part named "file", boundary ----FormBoundary<uuid>.
# No anthropic-beta, no anthropic-version. All HTTP errors swallowed.
# Requires the user:file_upload scope (server-enforced; never checked
# client-side). Trigger: SendUserMessage/Brief tool attachments.

# @name oauthFileUpload
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/oauth/file_upload
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----FormBoundary00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# The client also sets Content-Length explicitly to the assembled buffer's
# byte length. HTTP clients compute this themselves, so it is omitted here.
------FormBoundary00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="screenshot.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./screenshot.png
------FormBoundary00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000--

### Response:
# { "file_uuid": "..." }   // the only field read

### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2.6 OAuth File Download
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pattern: rg 'api/oauth/files' cli.js
#
# Host is BASE_API_URL only - ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL is IGNORED here, unlike
# the upload above. Timeout 30000 ms. Success is strictly HTTP 200.
# Read as an arraybuffer; no response header is inspected. No size limit,
# no retry. Trigger: inbound Remote Control message carrying
# file_attachments: [{ file_uuid, file_name }].
#
# NOT the public Files API - that is /v1/files/{id}/content, which sends
# anthropic-version and anthropic-beta: files-api-2025-04-14.

# @name oauthFileDownload
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/oauth/files/{{fileUuid}}/content
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Response: raw bytes

### ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
